#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# nest_graph

#% text
# `nest_graph(f, start, n)` gives the graph of repeated application of `f`: edges from each vertex `v` to the values of `f(v)`, for `n` levels.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `start` is one vertex or a list of vertices; `f(v)` is one vertex or a list of them.

#% item
# Level 0 is the starting vertices; each level adds the values of `f` on the vertices found at the previous one; the last level is not expanded. The default is one level, `inf` continues until no new vertex appears.

#% item
# Vertices come in the order they are found, edges in the order of their source vertices; an edge is listed once.

#% item
# The other options (`vertex_labels`, ...) go to `graph`; `directed_edges: false` makes the edges undirected.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
g = nest_graph(f, x, 3)
[vertex_list(g), edge_list(g)]
#% output
#= [[x, f(x), f(f(x)), f(f(f(x)))], [directed_edge(x, f(x)), directed_edge(f(x), f(f(x))), directed_edge(f(f(x)), f(f(f(x))))]]

#% text
# Two values at each step:

#% cell
edge_list(nest_graph(x => [f(x), h(x)], x0, 2))
#% output
#= [directed_edge(x0, f(x0)), directed_edge(x0, h(x0)), directed_edge(f(x0), f(f(x0))), directed_edge(f(x0), h(f(x0))), directed_edge(h(x0), f(h(x0))), directed_edge(h(x0), h(h(x0)))]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Starting from several vertices:

#% cell
edge_list(nest_graph(x => mod(x^2 + 1, 5), [0, 1, 2], 2))
#% output
#= [directed_edge(0, 1), directed_edge(1, 2), directed_edge(2, 0)]

#% text
# Until nothing new appears:

#% cell
vertex_list(nest_graph(x => if x < 4 then [x + 1, x + 2] else [], 1, inf))
#% output
#= [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

#% subsection
# Options

#% cell
edge_list(nest_graph(x => mod(x^2 + 1, 5), [0, 1, 2], 2, directed_edges: false))
#% output
#= [undirected_edge(0, 1), undirected_edge(1, 2), undirected_edge(2, 0)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `graph`, `vertex_list`, `edge_list`, `nest_list`
